  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1957-p42.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If \\(n\\) is even, \\(i^n\\) is \\(1\\) or \\(-1\\) and equals its reciprocal, so \\(S=2\\) or \\(-2.\\) If \\(n\\) is odd, the two terms are \\(i\\) and \\(-i,\\) in some order, so \\(S=0.\\) Thus the distinct values are \\[ -2,\\ 0,\\ 2, \\] three values.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Powers of \\(i\\) repeat with period four",
        "Check one representative of each residue class of \\(n\\) modulo \\(4\\)"
      ],
